* ''On the node, the pūlama marks the light and the session marks the face'' (operator, 2026-10-18, approving the house reading; light, lend, wear, 2026-11-17). The per-tab ask binds browser tabs; the human lights a node's faces at its pūlama once, each boot draws a lend from the pūlama with no route, and every CLI run, MCP seat and watcher proves its own face, one inside the lend, at the gate without asking again (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026`>> #/the-node-scope).

